{
  "id": "ticket_01KY93E3WYD13E71QM7GHWG1DE",
  "name": "session/transcript correctness: Codex wrong-transcript under concurrency; takeover fails-open on unreadable session",
  "slug": "session-transcript-correctness-codex-wrong-transcript-under",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "Codex exposes no session id, so locateCodex resolves by newest-mtime among cwd-matching rollouts — two concurrent Codex sessions in one cwd can attach the WRONG transcript to a session (silently wrong audit data, worse than null). Separately, start’s takeover check does readSession(active).catch(()=>null), so an unreadable active-session file makes start proceed as if nothing is active, overwriting active_session and abandoning the prior session with no takeover event.",
    "details_md": "",
    "acceptance": [
      "When two matching Codex rollouts are both newer than the session start, refuse to auto-attach and fall back to null+warning instead of guessing (and document the Codex limitation in --transcript guidance)",
      "start treats an unreadable recorded active session as an active session (fail closed: require --takeover, warn naming the file) rather than silently proceeding",
      "Tests cover both cases"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/sessions/transcript.ts:304-326 locateCodex (newest-mtime, unbounded scan inside lock)",
      "src/cli/commands/start.ts:139 readSession(...).catch(()=>null)"
    ],
    "meta": {},
    "v": 1
  },
